# There is no local database. The CRM is Turso and nothing in this repo opens a file, so these two
# lines describe an accident rather than a fixture: a hand-run dump or a debugging copy sitting in
# the working tree, full of real people, one `git add .` away from a public repo.
crm-export/
*.db*

.env.development
.env.*
!.env.example

# private/ is a local working directory and it stays out of git.
#
# It was tracked once, because what is in it had lived in a single sandbox and been lost, and git was
# the only durable place going. That is no longer true: it is rows in Turso now, read with
# `bun scripts/playbook.ts`. Tracking the files as well would be the second copy this project spent a
# lot of effort ending, and the copy that travels, because it is the one a clone carries.
#
# What is in there is not a credential, which is what makes it worse rather than better: a leaked key
# can be rotated in a minute and a named organisation cannot be unpublished. Nothing reads private/ at
# runtime, so an empty one breaks nothing.
private/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# claude code (machine-local)
#
# settings.json is ignored rather than tracked because it is a permission grant. It allows Bash,
# Write and Edit without a prompt, which is a reasonable local choice and a bad thing to hand a
# stranger who clones a public repository and opens an agent in it.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
